Otherwise it stays uncounted.
28. Edge-case protection rule
Any patch that fixes one provider/one path cannot silently break another
provider/path.
•
•
Example:
•
fixing FMP rows cannot break Finnhub rows.
29. Verification-before-patch rule
•
I will not patch from Claude wording alone.
•
I will always verify the live code path first.
30. Final-clean rule
•
Before creating a new version, I must work from one de-duplicated live ledger
only.
•
No patching from mixed notes.
What I cannot implement as a rule
•
I cannot create a process that guarantees a 100% perfect codebase.
•
I can reduce regression risk materially.
•
I can tighten the process so that false positives, silent regressions, and sloppy
patches are much less likely.
•
But “perfect” is not something I can honestly guarantee.
What I can do instead
•
Treat every single rule (count the total) as binding for the rest of this session.
•
•
Use them before the next patch.
Reject any patch that violates them even if the patch looks convenient.
31. Stop-on-ambiguity rule
•
If a bug fix would require choosing between two plausible interpretations of your
stock system, I stop and flag it instead of guessing.
